; walk-axx — `Axx` sets the speed from the row it sits on.
;
; `A03` on row 2 shortens THAT row (a tick-0 effect), and `A00` on row 3
; keeps what it found — IT gives `Axx` no memory. The second pass round
; the song runs at speed 3, so the walk plays seven rows for 27 ticks and
; the loop point is index 3, not index 4.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
